1. Spellcheck — real Hunspell WASM engine. The plugin is wired into the editor
   (createSpellcheckPlugin), but the checker behind it (SimpleSpellChecker,
   packages/editor/src/spellcheck/hunspell.ts) is an in-memory word-set placeholder:
   no .dic/.aff loading, and suggest() always returns []. Need to load real
   Hunspell dictionaries per language.
2. Language UI (low priority — display-only indicator done; full feature needs design):
   - One-click {lang=} override: right-click context menu, inserts tag at cursor or wraps selection
   - Language tags ({lang=XX}): not yet handled by parser/editor. Need to decide:
     a) AST representation in parser
     b) Editor rendering and preservation of tags
     c) How LanguageContext resolves effective language from tags vs frontmatter
     d) Whether tags apply to inline spans or whole block elements
3. Navigator color-coding by tags/location/status — not implemented; only a
   generic accent color exists for hover/selection, not data-driven coloring.
4. Watermark for exports — frontmatter watermark: renders on-screen and in
   print/PDF export (workflow-reports.ts), but is not applied in DOCX export
   (docx-exporter.ts). Also no per-export toggle to opt out when the field is
   set — it's implicitly always-on.
   DONE on branch feat/c1-print: the Word export puts the watermark (or the caller's
   override) in the header of every page; the opt-out toggle is still open.
10. @sutrata/cloud-connector (OSS spec §11.1, deferred): an open
    StorageAdapter for a documented sync API. Not planned for now; if built,
    it is not bundled by default and the app must work identically without it.
14. Import — legacy-font → Unicode conversion (OSS spec §5.5, §5.6, P2):
    Krutidev/Shree-Lipi for Hindi, Bamini/TAM/TAB for Tamil, Anu for Telugu
    first; then Nudi/Baraha, ML-TT. AI-assisted import of .docx/.txt/.md is
    done (packages/editor/src/import/).
18. Print paginator — page map and margin marks, for revision mode kept by an
    embedder (OSS spec §3.6, §11.3): PrintPaginationOptions has only content
    height, page-number prefix and CONTINUED suffix. Needed:
    - an optional fixed page map (locked page breaks), with new pages lettered
      as A-pages (12, 12A, 13) instead of reflowing later pages;
    - per-block margin marks (e.g. revision stars) and a per-page header label
      (e.g. revision color and date).
    Keep the default output unchanged when neither is given.
    DONE on branch feat/c1-print: locked pages are per scene (start and end page), see
    PrintPaginationOptions.lockedPages, PrintExtras and the `@sutrata/editor/dist/print.js` entry.
19. Scene number locking (OSS spec §8.6, P1): the "lock scene numbers" mode is
    specified but not implemented — once locked, Renumber letters new scenes
    only (a scene after 12 becomes 12A) and never changes an existing number.
    Also let SessionContext.featureFlags turn Renumber off (e.g. `renumber:
    false`), so an embedder can protect a locked script before the full mode
    exists; today the navigator's Renumber action is available to every edit
    session.
    DONE on branch feat/c1-print: featureFlags `renumber: false` and `lockSceneNumbers: true`.
